# Router held-out sample set (200 questions) for `tools/router_eval.py`.
#
# `(dataset, question_id)` pairs do not overlap the other router sample manifests.
# Question text is read through `benchmark_dir()` at runtime; it is not stored here.
#
# `expected_route` is human-labelled from `ROUTER_PROMPT` in
# `src/tianximem/retrieve/router.py`, not from dataset category fields.
#
# Current route classes:
# * `MULTI_HOP`: an unnamed intermediate entity or anchor must be resolved before the
#   remaining lookup can be expressed.
# * `DEFAULT`: all other queries, including comparisons where every entity is named.
#
# Legacy `COUNT` rows are retained in the fixture and skipped by the evaluator; current
# counting questions use grounded evidence before routing.
#
# `boundary: true` marks subjective cases. The evaluator reports them separately from
# the main confusion matrix. `DEFAULT` is intentionally more frequent than `MULTI_HOP`.
